  <result aggregation-status="1" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">SCS4 # of advocacy initiatives carried out by CSOs, for, by or with their membership/constituency</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN"># of advocacy initiatives carried out by CSOs, for, by or with their membership/constituency</narrative>
    </title>
    <reference code="SCS041" indicator-uri="https://helpdesk-opendata-minbuza.nl/indicator-codelist/" vocabulary="99"></reference>
    <baseline iso-date="2021-01-01" value="1" year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) Croix Rouge /Branche Buganda: Lobbying for improving access to health care services targeted at partners of the Red Cross including the Government of Burundi through the Ministry of Public Health and local administration. Requesting support for vulnerable people including persons with disabilities for access to health care through the granting of Health Insurance Cards (CAM). Identification of these people with the support of the local administration, mobilization of means to have the necessary number Health Insurance Cards and distribution of these CAMs to identified beneficiaries.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="20"></target>
     <actual value="0"></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
     <target value="20"></target>
     <actual value="7"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN"># of advocacy initiatives carried out by CSOs, for, by or with their membership/constituency at sub-national level</narrative>
    </title>
    <reference code="SCS042" indicator-uri="https://helpdesk-opendata-minbuza.nl/indicator-codelist/" vocabulary="99"></reference>
    <baseline iso-date="2021-01-01" value="9" year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) Garukira Abamugaye b&#x2019;i Mabayi: Awareness raising and lobbying for physical access to public buildings such as the hospital and the Mabayi Residence Court. 2) Garukira Abamugaye b&#x2019;i Mabayi Lobbying and awareness raising against the exploitation of disabled children by forcing them to beg at the Mabayi market. Raising awareness about the need for disabled children to go to school like other children. 3) ADEPH: Providing access to sport and recreational facilities through the redevelopment of a volleyball field into a Sitting Volleyball field with the possibility of playing both disciplines. 4) ADEPH: Lobbying for the inclusion of members of ADEPH as health data collectors for Community Health Centres in Buganda commune. Enhancement of data collection capacities. Requesting for official documents listing the status as health data collectors. The lobbying has led to the recognition of the value and inclusion of persons with disabilities in the health data collection teams. 5) ADEPH: Lobbying for the enrolment of members of ADEPH as community awareness actors during a 16 day mass awareness campaign against Gender Based Violence. 6) ADEPH: Changing negative attitude towards persons with disabilities by showing they have capacities. Various activities have been organized such as friendly matches with the Bubanza sitting volleyball team. The inclusion of persons with disabilities as awareness raising actors in the local theatre group. The skills training of persons with disabilities in basketry and bakery have demonstrated the capacities of persons with disabilities. 7) Croix Rouge /Branche Buganda: The organisation has contacted local authorities and advocated for decent housing of vulnerable persons including persons with disabilities. With the help of local authorities and the Red Cross authorities construction materials were collected and the construction of decent houses for vulnerable persons and persons with disabilities was started. 8) Croix Rouge /Branche Buganda: Raising awareness and lobbying for a change of language when referring to persons with disabilities. The word &quot;Ikimuga&quot; is commonly used when referring to persons with disabilities. This word is degrading as it means &#x201c;worthless&#x201d; and &#x201c;incapable&#x201d;. Awareness messages were developed for persons with disabilities on their capacities and rights to development in collaboration with the OPH ADEPH and displayed during sitting volleyball matches. 9) Association pour la R&#xe9;insertion des Handicap&#xe9;s-Twiyunge (ARH): Identification and mobilization of persons with disabilities in other areas for the establishment of ARH-Twiyunge branches in Gatwe and Kinzanza. Mobilization of membership fees and donations received from Handicap International.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="20"></target>
     <actual value="0"></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
     <target value="20"></target>
     <actual value="10"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
