   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">SCS3 # of times that CSOs succeed in creating space for CSO demands and positions through agenda setting, influencing the debate and/or creating space to engage</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN"># of times that CSOs succeed in creating space for CSO demands and positions through agenda setting, influencing the debate and/or creating space to engage at sub-national level</narrative>
    </title>
    <reference code="SCS032" indicator-uri="https://helpdesk-opendata-minbuza.nl/indicator-codelist/" vocabulary="99"></reference>
    <baseline iso-date="2021-01-01" value="3" year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) Garukira Abamugaye b&apos;i Mabayi The organisation launched a campaign directed to local authorities and community members in general to change devaluating language such as the word &apos;&apos;Ikimuga&apos;, which is a devaluing term for persons with disabilities, to something positive such as &apos;&apos;Umuntu agendana ubumuga&apos;&apos;, meaning a disabled person or a person living with a handicap in Kirundi. The organisation has used individual and mass sensitizations through music composed by a member of the OPH. 2) Croix Rouge /Branche Buganda To reduce the ill-treatment of Albino students by other students, the organisation has raised the awareness of school directors, municipal administrator, students and teachers about the rights and needs of pupils with albinism. In line with this the organisation has also conducted community awareness-raising visits to convince parents of newly born albino children of the rights, needs and capacities of persons with albinism. 3) Association pour la R&#xe9;insertion des Handicap&#xe9;s-Twiyunge (ARH) This organisation is targeting other organisations to put disability inclusion on the agenda with the aim of increasing acceptance and non-discrimination of persons with disabilities. The organisation facilitates the establishment of new associations and provides support in training other associations.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
